1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,320
There is a problem with handing
over a blockchain project.

2
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:06,475
Passing over files or making
an agreement does not transfer

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
the permissions that make the project run.

4
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:12,495
You need a clear way to pass
on control and understand what

5
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:17,035
access remains. Introducing Writ.
Writ turns a supported project

6
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:20,120
permission into a transferable digital key.

7
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:22,190
That key is an NFT.

8
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,575
Instead of only showing a picture,
it lets its current holder

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:29,245
carry out real actions. Here is
a simple example, using NEAR

10
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:33,280
Testnet and practice funds. Ada
runs an NFT collection, and

11
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:37,015
Ben is taking over. Ada opens
Writ, chooses the collection

12
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:40,240
administrator option, and
creates her Writ NFT.

13
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:43,305
She can use a compatible collection
she already controls, or

14
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:45,560
create a practice collection first.

15
00:00:45,610 --> 00:00:48,330
Writ then guides her through
the wallet approvals that give

16
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:51,920
the account behind the NFT
permission to manage the collection.

17
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:55,065
Creating the NFT and granting
that permission are separate

18
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:58,710
steps. Once that is complete,
Ada can issue a real collectible

19
00:00:58,890 --> 00:01:02,735
through Writ. She can also
inspect what the NFT allows, who

20
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:05,855
holds it, what money is available
in its control account, and

21
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:08,240
what temporary permissions have been granted.

22
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:11,120
The NFT can appear in a compatible wallet.

23
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:14,495
If Ada only wants someone to
perform a particular action, she

24
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:17,860
can lend that permission with
fixed details and an expiry.

25
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:21,780
She can cancel it. It can be used
repeatedly within those limits.

26
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:24,360
Now Ada sends the NFT to Ben.

27
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:28,260
No sale is required. Ben can
use its approved actions.

28
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:31,665
Ada loses her holder permission
through Writ, and the old temporary

29
00:01:31,690 --> 00:01:35,240
permissions are cancelled. The
collection itself stays in place,

30
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,960
with Ben now able to manage it through Writ.

31
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:41,085
This also works with the other
supported profiles: service

32
00:01:41,110 --> 00:01:44,735
ownership, voting through a DAO
council seat, token issuance,

33
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:47,360
and a treasury that pays out native NEAR.

34
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:50,990
Selling is optional. A buyer can
require the declared conditions

35
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:53,360
to pass before a purchase completes.

36
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:55,200
In this example, they fail.

37
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:58,635
The seller keeps the NFT, and the
buyer withdraws the purchase-price

38
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:02,345
refund. The disclosed record
charge and network fees still

39
00:02:02,370 --> 00:02:05,435
apply. Developers can connect
their own applications using

40
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:08,560
Writ's SDK, a small integration toolkit.

41
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:12,255
Here, Ben uses a separate
application, connects his own wallet,

42
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:15,615
and issues another collectible.
He does not need Writ's website

43
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,920
to exercise that permission.
For supported ownership roles,

44
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:21,870
Ben can also move control
directly into his wallet.

45
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:25,690
Writ checks the hand-back before
retiring the NFT, then lets

46
00:02:25,910 --> 00:02:29,280
him recover the remaining available
money in its control account.

47
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:32,855
Underneath, NEAR smart contracts
check the current holder before

48
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:36,605
forwarding an approved command.
The account behind the NFT

49
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:40,375
has no access keys. Separate
permissions outside Writ still

50
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:43,455
matter, and this testnet release
retains a collection upgrade

51
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:45,990
key. The app explains these limits.

52
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:49,360
Other contract interfaces
need reviewed integrations.

53
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:53,401
Writ. A digital key you can
use, lend, and hand over.
